          ====================================================================================================
          |                                CHARACTERISTICS OF THE SIMULATION                                 |
          ====================================================================================================
          |                                                                                                  |
          |                                     Type of simulation: NATU                                     |
          |                                                                                                  |
          | No stratification of source sampling                                                             |
          | Not necessarily sources placed for each cycle in each fissile set                                |
          | Not necessarily sources placed in a fissile set when it is visited                               |
          | Not necessarily sources placed for each cycle in each fissile set                                |
          | No calculation of the fission matrix during the active cycles                                    |
          | No calculation of the fission matrix during the inactive cycles                                  |
          | No use of the fission matrix eigenvector                                                         |
          | No use of the adjoint fission matrix eigenvector                                                 |
          | No weighting of the production with the importance function                                      |
          | Production in each fissile assembly estimated at the collisions                                  |
          | to calculate the new source distribution                                                         |
          | Potential fission sites created at the collisions                                                |
          | Initial keff estimate used to normalise the neutrons produced: 1.00000                           |
          | No simulation of decay products                                                                  |
          | No use of the Woodcock method                                                                    |
          | No use of splitting during volume changes                                                        |
          | Absorption simulation: death of neutron during absorption                                        |
          | No use of Russian roulette                                                                       |
          |                                                                                                  |
          | The simulation is performed between the following energies:                                      |
          | - Emin: 1.0000E-11 MeV                                                                           |
          | - Emax: 2.0000E+01 MeV                                                                           |
          | Continuous energy calculation, lattice of  256830 energies                                       |
          | Probability Tables are used for unresolved resonance range                                       |
          |                                                                                                  |
          |                                       Calculation of keff                                        |
          | Standard estimator  : BALANCE-TRACK-LENGTH                                                       |
